---
layout: changelog
title: Announcing Appwrite 2.7.2 for self-hosted deployments
date: 2026-11-12
cover: /images/changelog/2026-11-12.avif
tags: security, infrastructure
---

Appwrite 2.7.2 is now available for self-hosting. It is a security patch for the 2.7 line, and we recommend every 2.7 install upgrades.

This release includes:

- Security fixes across auth, abuse limits, storage, realtime, messaging, functions, VCS and proxy.
- Base image `appwrite/base` 2.2.11: patched git, curl, libexpat, perl, rsync and Docker CLI packages, and Go 1.27.4 for `git-remote-entire`.
- Console 1.2.181.

